 "_about": "When fruits and vegetables are in season across India, by climate zone. 'seasons' is the default for the plains (north, west, east); 'south' and 'cold_hill' override it where the climate differs (Kerala grows spinach all year, a Kashmir winter has haak, nadru and turnip but no bhindi). 'soft' items are stored or frozen everywhere all year (peas, apples), so they are never pushed down, only preferred in season. Sources: ICAR and state horticulture crop calendars, and the National Horticulture Board's seasonal availability notes. 'taseer' lists follow traditional Ayurvedic 'thanda' and 'garam' food beliefs; they are not medical evidence and are only used when a person switches them on.",
